  <section id="s1">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2>1. Relational Foundations: Interaction Networks and Spin-Network Holonomy</h2>
      <span class="mod-tag">chem/facts.cub · spin.cub · recoupling.cub · holonomy.cub · magloop.cub</span>
    </div>
    <p>In Carlo Rovelli's Relational Quantum Mechanics (RQM) and Loop Quantum Gravity (LQG), there is no primitive isolated substance and no background external clock: physical facts exist strictly relative to interactions between systems, and geometry is encoded in combinatorial graphs carrying group representations on edges and intertwiners on vertices.</p>
    <p>That ontology is identical to Hyperactivity's computational foundation. Just as an interaction-net cell has no hidden internal state outside the rules that fire when it meets another cell, a relational physical state is an observation record whose compatible histories form an observation fiber. The <code>chem/</code> library formalizes this first rung directly:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Spin networks &amp; recoupling (<code>chem/spin.cub</code>, <code>recoupling.cub</code>, <code>vertex.cub</code>):</strong> Exact combinatorial angular-momentum coupling, triangle inequalities, and recoupling identities checked over exact integers and rationals.</li>
      <li><strong>Holonomy &amp; magnetic flux loops (<code>chem/holonomy.cub</code>, <code>bholonomy.cub</code>, <code>magloop.cub</code>):</strong> Parallel transport around closed graph loops and Thiemann's \(U(1)\) magnetic operator acting strictly within quantized flux sectors — establishing gauge-invariant loop observables with machine-checked closure.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="s2">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2>2. Exact Relativistic Fine Structure: Dirac to Foldy–Wouthuysen</h2>
      <span class="mod-tag">chem/atom.cub · chem/dirac.cub · chem/fine.cub · chem/fineclaim.cub</span>
    </div>
    <p>Moving from discrete quantum geometry to atomic physics, the exact relativistic energy levels of a hydrogenic atom with nuclear charge \(Z\) and fine-structure constant \(\alpha\) are given by the Dirac–Sommerfeld formula:</p>
    $$E_{n,\kappa} \;=\; \frac{mc^2}{\sqrt{1 + \dfrac{(Z\alpha)^2}{\bigl(n - |\kappa| + \sqrt{\kappa^2 - (Z\alpha)^2}\bigr)^2}}} - mc^2$$
    <p>Expanding in powers of \(x = (Z\alpha)^2\) yields the non-relativistic Schrödinger level plus the three relativistic Foldy–Wouthuysen corrections — relativistic kinetic energy (\(p^4\)), the Darwin contact term, and spin–orbit coupling — which combine into a single exact rational coefficient:</p>
    $$\frac{E_{n,\kappa}}{mc^2} \;=\; -\frac{x}{2n^2} \;-\; \frac{x^2}{2n^4}\!\left(\frac{n}{|\kappa|} - \frac{3}{4}\right) \;+\; O(x^3)$$
    <div class="thm">
      <b>Checked Theorem — fine-to-n6 (chem/fineclaim.cub)</b>
      For every principal quantum number \(n \le 6\), orbital angular momentum \(l &lt; n\), and total angular momentum \(j = l \pm \tfrac{1}{2}\) (with \(\kappa = -(l+1)\) or \(+l\)), the exact formal power-series expansion of Dirac's formula matches the Foldy–Wouthuysen \(p^4 + \text{Darwin} + \text{spin–orbit}\) sum identically: <code>fn-all-ok 6 ≡ true</code>.
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="s3">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2>3. Zero-Float Ab Initio Quantum Chemistry: H₂ and Bareiss–Sylvester Helium</h2>
      <span class="mod-tag">chem/h2cert.cub · chem/bareisswit.cub · chem/sylvester.cub · chem/witnessclaim.cub</span>
    </div>
    <p>Standard quantum chemistry packages compute ground-state energies using floating-point eigensolvers (LAPACK) whose rounding errors are uncertified. Hyperactivity proves variational eigenvalue brackets using <strong>zero floating-point arithmetic</strong>:</p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Exact rational matrix elements:</strong> On a 7-function Hylleraas basis at nonlinear scale \(\alpha = 7/4\), the Hamiltonian matrix \(H\) and overlap matrix \(S\) are constructed over exact dyadic/rational arithmetic.</li>
      <li><strong>Bareiss fraction-free elimination (<code>chem/bareisswit.cub</code>):</strong> For any candidate energy shift \(\lambda\), the pencil \(H - \lambda S\) is reduced via exact integer Bareiss pivots without division drift.</li>
      <li><strong>Sylvester's Law of Inertia (<code>chem/sylvester.cub</code>, <code>inertiasound.cub</code>):</strong> The sign signature of the certified congruence diagonal counts the exact number of eigenvalues strictly below \(\lambda\). Proving \(0\) eigenvalues below \(\lambda_{\text{lo}}\) and \(\ge 1\) eigenvalue below \(\lambda_{\text{hi}}\) establishes an airtight mathematical bracket on the ground state.</li>
    </ol>
    <div class="thm">
      <b>Checked Certificate — he7-wit (chem/witnessclaim.cub)</b>
      The lowest Ritz eigenvalue of the 7-function Hylleraas Helium Hamiltonian is machine-certified in the exact dyadic interval:
      $$E_0(\mathrm{He}) \;\in\; \left[-\frac{3044409}{2^{20}},\; -\frac{3044408}{2^{20}}\right]\text{ Ha} \;=\; \bigl[-2.9033747,\; -2.9033737\bigr]\text{ Ha}$$
      checked directly in the cubical kernel with zero floating-point operations.
    </div>
<pre><code>he7-wit : wt-bracket (he-prob 7 4 he-b7) 0 (hc-negk 3044 409)
                     (hc-negk 3044 408) (true , bin-pow2 20) ≡ true</code></pre>
    <p>The same exact-witness architecture extends to the hydrogen molecular ion \(\mathrm{H}_2^+\) and neutral dihydrogen \(\mathrm{H}_2\) (`chem/h2plus.cub`, `chem/h2cert.cub`, `chem/h2ground.cub`).</p>
  </section>

  <section id="s4">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2>4. Many-Body Fermionic Algebra, SOS Positivity, and IMS Localization</h2>
      <span class="mod-tag">chem/fermiclaim.cub · chem/algebra.cub · chem/sosclaim.cub · chem/cut.cub</span>
