    <p>Over the tautomeric subset of the Cambridge Structural Database, Standard InChI achieves only a <strong>26.25%</strong> success rate (13.46% strict). Separating the three equalities with cubical paths and witness-carrying assay observations eliminates representation-induced database corruption at the root.</p>
