  <section id="s6">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2>6. Living Matter: Metamorphic Folds, Compositional Basins, and Bioelectric Morphogenesis</h2>
      <span class="mod-tag">chem/fold.cub · chem/basin-compose.cub · neuro/barrier.cub · docs/michael-levin-and-hyperactivity.md</span>
    </div>
    <p>The top rung of the physical ladder bridges quantum/chemical dynamics directly into multi-scale living systems and Michael Levin's theory of bioelectric morphogenesis and cognitive light cones:</p>

    <h3>6.1 Compositional Attractor Basins and Metamorphic Folds</h3>
    <p>In <code>chem/basin-compose.cub</code>, a dynamical system's attractor basin is constructed as a Higher Inductive Type (<code>basin-of</code>) quotienting states along flow steps. We prove functoriality of flow homomorphisms (<code>basin-map</code>, <code>basin-map-id</code>, <code>basin-map-comp</code>), flow refinement when new transitions open (<code>basin-refine</code>), coupled-subsystem merging (<code>basin-prod-coupled</code>, <code>basin-couple-merges</code>), and <strong>metamorphic folds</strong> (<code>MetaFold</code>) where a single underlying substrate switches attractor topologies without losing identity.</p>

    <h3>6.2 Exact Bioelectric Dissipation Splitting (Isopotential Domain Collapse)</h3>
    <p>Consider two cells with resting potential \(E\), membrane leak conductance \(g &gt; 0\), and gap-junction coupling conductance \(g_c \ge 0\). Their total bioelectric dissipation functional is \(D(V_1, V_2) = g(V_1 - E)^2 + g(V_2 - E)^2 + g_c(V_1 - V_2)^2\). In <code>neuro/barrier.cub</code>, <code>bioelectric-gap-split-sos-id</code> proves the exact universal orthogonal decomposition over \(\mathbb{Q}\):</p>
    $$2\Bigl(g(V_1 - E)^2 + g(V_2 - E)^2 + g_c(V_1 - V_2)^2\Bigr) \;=\; g\,(V_1 + V_2 - 2E)^2 \;+\; (g + 2g_c)\,(V_1 - V_2)^2$$
    <div class="thm">
      <b>Biological Meaning — Cognitive Light-Cone Merging vs. Cancer Decoupling</b>
      When gap junctions are open (\(g_c &gt; 0\)), the voltage-difference mode \((V_1 - V_2)\) dissipates at the accelerated rate \(g + 2g_c\), collapsing the two cells onto a single collective isopotential quotient \(V_1 = V_2\) — expanding their shared morphogenetic boundary (<code>basin-couple-merges</code>). When gap junctions close (\(g_c \to 0\), as in oncogenesis or gap-junction blockers), the cross-term vanishes and each cell collapses back into its own isolated local basin.
    </div>
